  "finding": "Annex VI Article 4 controls the Dutch full-time Notarial Law route. It requires 175 EC and one linked 4 EC metajuridical perspective plus 1 EC essay, with no open elective block. Criminology is selected by first official listing. Private Law, State and Administrative Law, and Criminal Procedure are progression foundations. First-year tutoring is required without separate credit. Thesis entry requires the three academic skills units; the thesis regulation sets registration, group meetings, and a 4000–5000 word thesis. Part-time and historical substitutions do not enter the selected route."
}
